a seismic shift is happening within the  meat industry  social and economic trends like food  inflation and growing inequality  are converging with a rising  preference for plant-based diets  and that all together is impacting how  we consume meat  in many countries the pandemic has  shrunk people's wallets  problems with supply chains as well as  tight market for animal feed have  combined to  spark meat inflation while we are still  waiting for data to come through  interviews with many families from  around the world uh  confirmed that more and more people are  struggling  to obtain meat so have you reduced  your meat consumption or issues  even in the wealthier parts of the world  more people are getting priced out of  meat  in new york income is a stark driver of  meat spending  americans are now spending less on meat  at grocery stores  than they were at the start of the year  of course demand for meat  dipped during the past economic crisis  only to rebound but what is new this  time  it's happening at the same time as  consumers  are increasingly shifting to plant-based  diets  well we have seen an increase in the  retail demand  you know we grew 300 last year this  despite the  you know the pandemic i think  plant-based has has two  two good reasons to to keep going very  strong one is  environmental reasons and the second one  is now i would say personal  health and nutrition more conscious than  ever of meat's impact on the planet  human health and animal welfare a  growing number of middle class consumers  are reaching out for plant-based  alternatives  some estimates point to reduced spending  particularly for premium meats such as  beef  the most polluting animal product  in germany the number of vegetarians and  vegans doubled during the pandemic  while in france almost half of people  reduce meat intake in the last three  years  plant-based trends aren't limited to the  western world in china it's catching on  among the youth and can be seen at  trendy and upscale restaurants  all taken together this signals a  substantial shift for the meat industry  and offers some hope for a reduction in  global greenhouse gas emissions  of which meat is a major source but for  those struggling to make ends meet  not being able to afford meat often  means not having access to a key source  of nutrients in their diet  changes to the diet of brazilians  reflect the economic toll  from the pandemic and they also ripple  across emerging and developing countries  which until now have been viewed as the  major driver  of meat demand growth  [Music]  [Music]  foreign
 

